+/*
+ * USB mux (pclink, boot-arg pong_usb_mux; work/pclink_scope/PLAN.md). Bit 0 adds a vendor interface FF/FE/02 with one
+ * bulk pair (EP5 OUT/IN) after the CDC function(s): the usbmux interface a PC's usbmuxd claims. pong_usbmux.c speaks
+ * the protocol and connects each stream to 127.0.0.1:<port> (lockdownd 62078). The device is composite (IAD), PID
+ * 0x316f (0x3170 with NCM), and answers Microsoft OS 1.0 descriptors so Windows binds WinUSB to the mux interface by
+ * itself. Bit 1 sends VID 05AC PID 12AB instead, the id libimobiledevice's usbmuxd and macOS look for.
+ * The DMA buffer grows to 128 KiB; the mux uses only 0x5400-0x55ff and 0x10000-0x17fff.
+ */
